1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4 d5 4. fxe5 Nxe4 5. Qh5? { Looks tempting because the queen eyes the pawn on f7 and the knight on e4, but Black simply kicks it with ...g6. } 5... g6 6. Qf3 { The queen must retreat. } 6... Bg7 7. Nxe4 dxe4 8. Qxe4 { White has the pawn back but Black is better developed and has the safer king. Develop with Nf3 first, as in the main line. } *
